.SH CLI OVERVIEW & GLOBAL FLAGS
.PP
The \fBcf\fR CLI follows a standard syntax:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf <resource> <action> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Global Flags"
.PP
Every command supports the following global flags:
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--profile <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBstring\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Use a specific profile configured in \fB~/.cf/config.json\fR
.TP
\fB--output <format>\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBstring\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Output format: \fBtable\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBcsv\fR, \fByaml\fR
.TP
\fB--raw\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Print raw, unformatted API JSON response
.TP
\fB--verbose\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Print HTTP request URLs, methods, headers, and timing
.TP
\fB--quiet\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Suppress non-essential informational and progress messages
.TP
\fB--no-color\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Disable colored terminal output (also respects \fBNO_COLOR=1\fR)
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Automatically confirm destructive actions (e.g., delete)
.TP
\fB--help\fR, \fB-h\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Show command syntax and help
.TP
\fB--version\fR, \fB-v\fR
\fIType:\fR \fBboolean\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Show current CLI version
.RE
.PP
.PP
